iso classes: {3: 2, 4: 4, 5: 12, 6: 56}

==========================================================================================
(1)+(3)  ζ_T(u)=1/det(I-uA);  det(I-uA)=Σ c_j u^j = ∏ over strong components; ζ=1 on acyclic
==========================================================================================
  det(I-uA)=∏_SCC det over all 74 classes n<=6: mismatches=0
  transitive n=5: det(I-uA)=[1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]  => ζ=1 (no closed orbits; A nilpotent)
  => ζ_T is INVISIBLE to the acyclic part; all content is in the strong components (strong-core reduction).

==========================================================================================
(2)  EULER PRODUCT: prime-cycle counts π_ℓ=(1/ℓ)Σ_{d|ℓ}μ(ℓ/d)N_d are non-neg integers
==========================================================================================
  prime-cycle counts π_ℓ non-negative for all classes n<=6: True
  3-cycle atom: det(I-uA)=[1, 0, 0, -1] => ζ=1/(1-u^3); N_k=[0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 3]; prime cycles π={3: 1} (one length-3 prime)

==========================================================================================
(4) complement-invariance ζ_T=ζ_{T^op}   (5) N_3 = 3·c3
==========================================================================================
  det(I-uA(T)) == det(I-uA(T^op)) for all classes n<=6 (=> ζ complement-invariant): True
  N_3 = tr(A^3) = 3*c3 for all classes n<=6: True   (c3 is read off ζ's u^3 log-coefficient)

==========================================================================================
(6) circulant atoms: N_k=Σ_j λ_j^k (trig/character moments); ζ poles at 1/λ_j
==========================================================================================
  Paley- 7: N_1,N_2,N_3 (trace) = [0, 0, 42] ; Σλ_j^k = [0, 0, 42] ; match=True ; poles 1/λ have |λ|=√7=2.646 (non-Perron)
  Paley-11: N_1,N_2,N_3 (trace) = [0, 0, 165] ; Σλ_j^k = [0, 0, 165] ; match=True ; poles 1/λ have |λ|=√11=3.317 (non-Perron)
  Paley-19: N_1,N_2,N_3 (trace) = [0, 0, 855] ; Σλ_j^k = [0, 0, 855] ; match=True ; poles 1/λ have |λ|=√19=4.359 (non-Perron)

  => ζ_T is the closed-orbit generating function; its Euler product lives on the strong core,
     its poles are reciprocals of the trigonometric atom-spectra (Gauss sums / Chebyshev).
